{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {green}News {grey}- Dec 3rd, 2019{bold0}
{size0}{black}- A.R.S.E.N.A.L Extended Power still alive!

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Dec 15th, 2010{bold0}
{size0}{black}- v2.H allow to migrate to the {bold1}new game server{bold0}.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Mar 7th 2009{bold0}
{size0}{black}- {bold1}World High Score{bold0} has been moved. Check the new graphical world records interface from the game menu 'Records' then click 'World Record'.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Feb 21st 2009{bold0}
{size0}{black}- This launcher upgrade provides new support for lost licenses recovery. Redundant {bold1}Questions & Answers{bold0} are replaced with 'Frequently Asked Questions'. From now on users are invited to use the game 'Chat room' to post messages.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {green}News {grey}- July 23rd, 2007{bold0}
{size0}{black}- Cool A.R.S.E.N.A.L on-line veterans invit all players for a just for fun tournament on {blueink}{bold1}Saturday the 4th of August{black}{bold0} all day long.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {green}News {grey}- May 16th, 2007{bold0}
{size0}{black}- The Game Editor Agreement includes from now on a new article: "Tactical Soft disapprove the design of games with only concern of gaining large scores without significant difficulty. Such games don't respect this game motto 'Triumph without peril brings no glory' and therefore will be removed from game server"

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {green}News {grey}- Apr 19th, 2007{bold0}
{size0}{black}- {bold1}Windows Vista compatibility{bold0} : To have A.R.S.E.N.A.L Extended Power running under Windows Vista you just need to copy the file c:\windows\system32\dplay.dll from Windows XP system into game folder on Vista system.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Feb 12th 2007{bold0}
{size0}{black}- A new names list for units : {blueink}{bold1}Greek names{black}{bold0} provided by Christian von Irle, including famous names like Ulyss, Socrates, Xenakis and many more.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Oct 26th 2006{bold0}
{size0}{black}- Game version {red}{bold1}2.EP{bold0}{black} fixes a problem with loading games from User Games Server.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- May 16th, 2006{bold0}
{size0}{black}- From launcher version 1.C passport for on-line game can be bought without buying a game license. Also this upgrade supports a new client service : backup/restoring of the player file to/from Tactical Soft server.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- May 1st, 2006{bold0}
{size0}{black}- 2.Ej version fixes some bugs with on-line game connection interface.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Apr 15th, 2006{bold0}
{size0}{black}- 2.Ei upgrade introduces a new game loading interface that gives access to users game levels server from solo game and on-line game.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Apr 3rd, 2006{bold0}
{size0}{black}- This update features the Alliances Board (hot key A) and the Player Table (hot key Z). A bug with new modes and multi-players has been fixed.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Mar 25th, 2006{bold0}
{size0}{black}- The 2.Eg introduces 6 new game modes for multi-player or solo matches, with presetable time limit. Also blame and demotion penalties have been removed.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Mar 11th, 2006{bold0}
{size0}{black}- With 2.Ee version you may now watch the {red}LIVE{black} on-line games. Watchers are also allowed to send messages to players.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Jan 29th, 2006{bold0}
{size0}{black}- From 2.Ed update diplomatic actions and using mass destruction weapons will affect player reputation in real time, while these actions won't affect player score nor score multipliers anymore.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Jan 20th, 2006{bold0}
{size0}{black}- The 2.Ec update allows to play {blueink}A.R.S.E.N.A.L ON-LINE{black} from slow Internet connections like dial modems without blocking the other players.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Dec 13th, 2005{bold0}
{size0}{black}- The 2.E update allows on-line games without disabling firewalls. {red}When you want to play on-line with others and there's nobody on-line you need to CREATE a game session and wait for others to JOIN your game.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- June 28th, 2005{bold0}
{size0}{black}- 2.Df provides improvements for the Deep View in true color mode, add-on to download: new image bank {blueink}Plain buildings{black}.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- May 3rd, 2005{bold0}
{size0}{black}- 2.De update allows screen shots in BMP format and true colors. Shortcut {blueink}CTRL+F1.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Apr 22nd, 2005{bold0}
{size0}{black}- Version 2.Dc supports the Deep View for all display modes. Check {blueink}Game Options > Display Mode.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Mar 30th, 2005{bold0}
{size0}{black}- With version 2.D all true color video modes are supported. New image banks in true colors are to be downloaded from the {blueink}Add-on section.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Feb 3rd, 2005{bold0}
{size0}{black}- On the way to true colors version 2.CC supports all available display sizes, check: {blueink} Game Options > Display Size

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Jan 15th, 2005{bold0}
{size0}{black}- A new display option allows to extend the game vision : {blueink} Options > Display Options > Deep View

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Nov 9th, 2004{bold0}
{size0}{black}- Camp generator available from level editor.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Oct 30th, 2004{bold0}
{size0}{black}- Upgrade introducing way points for factories and shipyards. Few improvements in the AI combat engine.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Aug 16th, 2004{bold0}
{size0}{black}- This update introduces a new adjustable game parameter allowing units to go repair automatically (check Game Options folder).

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Aug 1st, 2004{bold0}
{size0}{black}- Gas trucks and fire engines will now work for allies as well.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- July 20th, 2004{bold0}
{size0}{black}- With this update allied territories have become automatically visible.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- June 25th, 2004{bold0}
{size0}{black}- Civilians will now surrender to occupying forces which avoid to have to destroy housings.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- June 12th, 2004{bold0}
{size0}{black}- In game a chat room, hotkey CTRL ENTER, let you know who is there for on-line game, plus 3 new ranks above Marshal.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- June 1st, 2004{bold0}
{size0}{black}- Yearly subscription allowing 10 license recoveries without backup and access to Random Game Generator OFF LINE.

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- May 2nd, 2004{bold0}
{size0}{black}- Random game generator available for on-line games: {blueink}Play > Custom Game > On-line Game

{size200}{grey}{bold1}Tactical {red}Update {grey}- Mar 26th, 2004{bold0}
{size0}{black}- RANDOM GAME GENERATOR released providing huge game depth with billions of custom games automatically generated.
